Since you're spoiled...

Do you have teleportitis?  Wizards have intrinsic teleport control,
and bouncing across the levels of Gehennom is _way_ faster than
walking.  You'll still want to dig paths on the no-teleport levels.

In the same vein, a handful of cursed scrolls of teleportation will
aid your speed. Use one to get from Rodney to the VS level, then a b/u
scroll or ^T to get to the square, invoke, and another cursed scroll
to the Sanctum level will bypass a lot of intervening annoyances. Once
you have the amulet, cursed gain level up and out of the Sanctum to
avoid the same annoyances.

You don't need more levels at this point unless you want to max out
your MM damage.  If you're going to go for levels, I'd save the gain
level potions and go consort with some foocubi.  Besides being
generally safe with your stats (wear a +2 adornment ring if you want
perfectly safe), you can get far more levels that way than you could
from potions.

Do you have a means of detecting the elemental portals? The most
common is probably confused scrolls of gold detection, but if you have
a crystal ball you can also search for ^.

For grins, do you have conflict?  Astral gets much easier when
everyone is fighting everyone else.

Lastly, do you have the spell of jumping?  That plus very fast speed
lets you sprint through the ascension run while your enemies are
eating your dust.  A light source is critical to getting maximum
effectiveness from jumping--preferably a magic lamp or the candlabrum
(which will run out of candles quickly).



